CommitDate: Sat Nov 7 14:19:39 2026 +0000

    Require distinct producer generations and case-bound evidence for closure
    
    Independent reviews rejected both earlier continuity repairs: repeated probes
    over unchanged snapshots, and content hashes of state files (including the case
    index that reconciliation itself rewrites), do not prove independent fresh
    observations.
    
    Health rows now record the evidence generation as each producer's own
    observed_at (leg, exe, jud, out, meas, inn). Excluded: institutional-cases/
    index.json, which this reconciler mutates, so our own bookkeeping cannot
    manufacture a generation.
    
    Continuity cases additionally require their own pre-existing, Judiciary-scoped
    reconciliation receipt and record it as closure_evidence; generic health
    recovery alone cannot discharge a continuity obligation.
    
    Tests add: identical producers over two probes cannot close; a real producer
    re-observation can; a malformed/arbitrary token cannot; index.json churn does
    not change the generation; continuity closure cites the case-specific receipt;
    withdrawing the receipt keeps the case open.

